{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462581-lunacy-and-the-oath-of-the-moon-on-human-packmates","id":462581,"title":"Lunacy and the Oath of the Moon on Human packmates.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T12:24:38-07:00","id":462581,"title":"Lunacy and the Oath of the Moon on Human packmates.","content":"With human packmates, whether peripherally part of the pack or brought in temporarily using the Dominance facet Lead the Lesser Pack. I assume they're subject to lunacy as per usual. Are there any resistances? And is it a violation of the Oath of the Moon to let either of these groups of humans in on the knowledge of the Uratha? I mean once the facet wears off the humans don't seem to forget anything that happened so they could go on to just tell everyone they know about werewolves, right? It seems risky as hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:36:32-07:00","id":462607,"title":"","content":"See the pack rite &quot;Luna's Mad Love&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:46:44-07:00","id":462611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462581-lunacy-and-the-oath-of-the-moon-on-human-packmates#post462581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With human packmates, whether peripherally part of the pack or brought in temporarily using the Dominance facet Lead the Lesser Pack. I assume they're subject to lunacy as per usual. Are there any resistances? And is it a violation of the Oath of the Moon to let either of these groups of humans in on the knowledge of the Uratha? I mean once the facet wears off the humans don't seem to forget anything that happened so they could go on to just tell everyone they know about werewolves, right? It seems risky as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes they're subject to Lunacy, unless you do something about it.<br /> <br /> Whether it's a violation would depend on the belief system of the people doing the judging and the attitude of the werewolves with the humans. If you just have for instance your mother as a human member of the pack, simply because you're protecting her but otherwise keeping her out of all the details, ideally you would be able to convince her not to drag you onto Springer and announce to all her child's a werewolf. But if they were distant and intractable you might have a problem, similar to the Wayne Enterprises employee who suspected Bruce Wayne was Batman in <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0468569/\" target=\"_blank\">the Dark Knight</a> movie. Having packmates like that can be a risk, but it can be one worth taking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:05:24-07:00","id":462625,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't personally count packmates as part of &quot;The Herd&quot; who Must Not Know. That seems to be a general thing referring to humanity at large, and anyone you would call a packmate is probably trustworthy enough to be let in on it without risking the secret getting out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:30:49-07:00","id":462674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462581-lunacy-and-the-oath-of-the-moon-on-human-packmates#post462581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With human packmates, whether peripherally part of the pack or brought in temporarily using the Dominance facet Lead the Lesser Pack. I assume they're subject to lunacy as per usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there any resistances? </div> </div> </div>Some. The Moon's Mad Love Rite will help. Also note that groups working together towards a goal gain a bonus to their dice pool to resist - and the humans in a pack will frequently be working towards the pack's goals when they are exposed to Lunacy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And is it a violation of the Oath of the Moon to let either of these groups of humans in on the knowledge of the Uratha? I mean once the facet wears off the humans don't seem to forget anything that happened so they could go on to just tell everyone they know about werewolves, right? It seems risky as hell. </div> </div> </div>It is risky, yes. Is it a violation? That's the sort of thing Uratha would argue about a lot.<br /> <br /> <i>Broadly speaking</i>, bringing the humans in your pack into the know won't be a violation of the Oath, unless you do so knowing full well they're the sort to immediately go blab about it/spread the information around unsafely/etc. Bringing humans fully into the know who have been added via Lead the Lesser Pack, however, is a much more debatable case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:35:26-07:00","id":462677,"title":"","content":"That all makes sense. That's about what I figured but I totally missed the Moon's Mad Love rite. That'll help things a lot, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}